        <h2>How ConvertKB Compresses Multi-Page PDFs Without Quality Destruction</h2>
        <p>
          Many tools simply attempt to clear metadata from a PDF file. However, metadata stripping only saves 2 to 5 KB. When a PDF contains multiple scanned pages or high-resolution images, true compression requires full raster downsampling:
        </p>
        
        <h3>1. Virtual Page Rendering (PDF.js Engine)</h3>
        <p>
          ConvertKB reads the binary bytecode of your document and feeds it to Mozilla's PDF.js runtime. Each page's vector and bitmap content is drawn onto a dedicated offscreen canvas at a calculated target viewport scale. This flattens bloated layer hierarchies, embedded transparency masks, and duplicate font subsets.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Iterative Discrete Cosine Transform (DCT) Quantization</h3>
        <p>
          The rendered canvas frame is encoded into a high-efficiency JPEG byte stream. High-frequency image noise that the human eye cannot discern on mobile screens or standard monitors is systematically eliminated. For text documents, our Grayscale Mode extracts luminance channels while whitening grayish backgrounds, cutting file weights by up to 80% while retaining crisp font edges.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Document Reassembly (PDF-Lib &amp; jsPDF)</h3>
        <p>
          The compressed page streams are recompiled into a lightweight PDF container using PDF-Lib. Unreferenced object identifiers are dropped, resulting in a portable PDF that uploads cleanly to strict submission portals without rejection errors.
        </p>

        <h2>Complete Image Studio Capabilities</h2>
        <p>
          Preparing candidate photographs involves more than hitting a file size target:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cropper Presets:</strong> Instantly lock framing to 1:1 (Visa / UPSC), 3.5:4.5 (Passport / SSC), or 2:1 (Signature) ratios.</li>
          <li><strong>Document Whiten / High Contrast:</strong> Scanned certificates and signatures often have grayish or shadowy paper backgrounds. The High Contrast mode eliminates ambient shadows and ensures ink stands out clearly on a pure white field.</li>
          <li><strong>DPI Metadata Injection:</strong> Portals like NSDL PAN verify document resolution headers. Set your file to 200 DPI or 300 DPI directly in our controls.</li>
          <li><strong>Aspect Ratio Preservation:</strong> Lock explicit pixel widths without vertical or horizontal stretching.</li>
